## [Narrative Battle Report](/archive/recaps/s2-battle-report-reclaiming-book-of-st-lucius)

Check out a narrative battle report of Carson's Sisters of Argent Shroud against Paul's Plague Marines.

Games will be Narrative Play (Crusade) using Power Level instead of points.  The goal of the campaign is to have your faction obtain the highest [Strategic Value](https://wahapedia.ru/wh40k9ed/the-rules/charadon/#Winning-the-Campaign).  To determine the winner of each campaign phase war zone points will be awarded - scoring will be dictated based on game size and winner via [War Zone points](https://wahapedia.ru/wh40k9ed/the-rules/charadon/#War-Zone-Points) from War Zone: Charadon Act I: The Book of Rust.  You can view the war zone scoring via [Wahapedia](https://wahapedia.ru/wh40k9ed/the-rules/charadon/#War-Zone-Points).  In addition to war zone points for battle size; during each phase of the campaign all players will generate a [Secret Order](https://wahapedia.ru/wh40k9ed/the-rules/charadon/#Secret-Orders) by rolling a D6 and submit a prediction via Warseers and Portents.  Once per campaign phase players may play that phases legendary mission for an additional War Zone point (phase one - [Rout on Okharium](https://wahapedia.ru/wh40k9ed/the-rules/charadon/#Rout-on-Okharium); phase two - [Flood Tide on Fathom](https://wahapedia.ru/wh40k9ed/the-rules/charadon/#Flood-Tide-on-Fathom); phase three - [Desperation and Despair](https://wahapedia.ru/wh40k9ed/the-rules/charadon/#Desperation-and-Despair)).

